  "description": "Determine if a cycle exists in a 2D grid containing characters where a cycle is a path of length 4 or more with the same character.",
  "target": null,
  "pseudocode": "1. function hasCycle(grid):\n2.   visited = set()\n3.   for r in rows: for c in cols:\n4.     if (r, c) not in visited:\n5.       if dfs(r, c, -1, -1, grid[r][c], visited): return true\n6.   return false\n7. function dfs(r, c, pr, pc, char, visited):\n8.   visited.add((r, c))\n9.   for dr, dc in directions:\n10.    nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n11.    if valid(nr, nc) and grid[nr][nc] == char:\n12.      if (nr, nc) in visited and (nr, nc) != (pr, pc): return true\n13.      if (nr, nc) not in visited and dfs(nr, nc, r, c, char, visited): return true\n14.  return false",
